 think expected_revision_id should be the current revision id to guard against concurrent edits.\n\nLet me redo with the current revision id."}},{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"text","text":"The edit didn't apply — I passed a stale `expected_revision_id`. Using the current revision id:"}},{"type":"block-end","index":2,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_n6aVrZH6v5bUr8gLetTd4534","name":"edit_dut","arguments":"{\"expected_revision_id\": \"f62e2c19-1f68-4df8-8eb2-588dadbe2352\", \"source\": \"module TopModule (\\n    input c,\\n    input d,\\n    output [3:0] mux_in\\n);\\n    assign mux_in[0] = c | d;\\n    assign mux_in[1] = 1'b0;\\n    assign mux_in[2] = c | ~d;\\n    assign mux_in[3] = c & d;\\nendmodule\\n\"}"}},{"type":"usage","usage":{"inputTokens":12418,"outputTokens":663,"totalTokens":13849,"cacheReadTokens":768,"reasoningTokens":481}},{"type":"finish","reason":{"kind":"tool-calls"}}]